                <pb facs="0649" n="561" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg561"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hirsch to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1891-04-20"><hi rendition="#italic">April 20, 1891</hi></date>.
                        (Received May 5.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 432.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my No. 397 of February 29,
                    1892, and No. 424 of April 3, 1892, in relation to detention of letters
                    addressed to Americans in this empire, I now have the honor of reporting that
                    instructions have gone from the Sublime Porte to all the post-office officials
                    not to permit any detentions of letters addressed to Americans.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Solomon Hirsch.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
